Core Idea:

Early IP Fetch in main.go: After determining the nodeRole and loading the initial configuration (via config.LoadConfigurationViper), we'll fetch the public IP using net_utils.fetchPublicIPFromIPInfo().
Store in Role's Config: The fetched IP information (full JSON response) will be added to the *config.Config struct and then saved back to the role-specific configuration file (e.g., ~/.config/KNIRVROOT/root_data/root_config.json or ~/.config/KNIRVROOT/dev_data/dev_config.json). We'll use the existing config.SaveConfigToUserDir which leverages config.SaveMinimalConfig.
Eliminate env.local for IP: Remove the logic in install.go and net_utils.go that writes IP-related info to any env.local files.
ROOTCHAIN_URL Update: For the Root role, ROOTCHAIN_URL in constants.go will be updated using the fetched public IP.
Frontend Access: altgui will expose an API endpoint that reads the IP information from the *config.Config struct (which now contains the IP info). The Next.js frontend will call this API.
